  "title": "COVID-19, Influenza, and RSV Wastewater Monitoring in the U.S. | Week of March 21, 2026",
  "summary": "Summary: Week of 3/21/26 Biobot’s national network shows that SARS-CoV-2, influenza A, and influenza B are decreasing nationally, while RSV is increasing, driven by increases in the South and Midwest. This has been one of the longest RSV seasons in recent history, causing some states (like California) to extend the recommendation window for infant […]",
